"Internal Error ()\nciteturn2view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/2435\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/2435 is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncq: Cached quotients for fast lookups (https://eprint.iacr.org/2022/1763)\nciteturn2view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2022/1763\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 76\nL0: # What a lovely hat\nL1: #### Is it made out of 【0†tin foil†iacr.org】?\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Cryptology ePrint Archive】\nL4: \nL5:   * 【2†Papers】 Updates from the last:\nL6:     * 【3†7 days】\nL7:     * 【4†31 days】\nL8:     * 【5†6 months】\nL9:     * 【6†365 days】\nL10:     * * * *\nL11: \nL12:     * 【7†Listing by year】\nL13:     * 【8†All papers】\nL14:     * 【9†Compact view】\nL15:     * 【10†Subscribe†www.iacr.org】\nL16:     * * * *\nL17: \nL18:     * 【11†How to cite】\nL19:     * * * *\nL20:     * 【12†Harvesting metadata】\nL21:   * 【2†Submissions】\nL22:     * 【13†Submit a paper】\nL23:     * 【14†Revise or withdraw a paper】\nL24:     * 【15†Acceptance and publishing conditions】\nL25: \nL26: 【16†Image: Search Button】\nL27: \nL28: [Input] [Button: Search ]\nL29: #### Paper 2022/1763\nL30: \nL31: ### 【17†cq: Cached quotients for fast lookups】\nL32: \nL33: Liam Eagen, Blockstream\nL34: \nL35: Dario Fiore, IMDEA Software\nL36: \nL37: Ariel Gabizon, Zeta Function Technologies\nL38: ##### Abstract\nL39: We present a protocol called $\\mathsf{cq}$ for checking the values of a committed polynomial $f(X)\\in \\mathbb{F}_{<n}(X)$ over a multiplicative subgroup $H\\subset \\mathbb{F}$ of size $n$ are contained in a table $t\\in \\mathbb{F}^N$. After an $O(N \\log N)$ preprocessing step, the prover algorithm runs in time $O(n\\log n)$.\nL40: Thus, we continue to improve upon the recent breakthrough sequence of results [ZBKMNS,PK,GK,ZGKMR] starting from $\\mathsf{Caulk}$ [ZBKMNS], which achieve sublinear complexity in the table size $N$. The two most recent works in this sequence $\\mathsf{Ba}\\mathit{loo}$ [ZGKMR] and $\\mathsf{flookup}$ [GK] achieved prover complexity $O(n\\log^2 n)$. Moreover, $\\mathsf{cq}$ has the following attractive features. 1.\nL41: As in [ZBKMNS,PK,ZGKMR] our construction relies on homomorphic table commitments, which makes them amenable to vector lookups. 2. As opposed to the previous four works, our verifier doesn't involve pairings with prover defined $\\mathbb{G}_2$ points, which makes recursive aggregation of proofs more convenient.\nL42: Note: Fixes by Marek\nL43: ##### Metadata\nL44: \nL45: Available format(s)\nL46:     【17†PDF】\nL47: Category\nL48:     【18†Cryptographic protocols】\nL49: Publication info\nL50:     Preprint.\nL51: Keywords\nL52:     【19†zk-snarks】【20†lookup protocols】\nL53: Contact author(s)\nL54:     ariel gabizon @ gmail com\nL55: History\nL56:     2024-07-05: last of 5 revisions\nL57:     2022-12-25: received\nL58:     【21†See all versions】\nL59: Short URL\nL60:     【22†https://ia.cr/2022/1763†ia.cr】\nL61: License\nL62: \nL63: 【23†CC0†creativecommons.org】\nL64: BibTeX 【24†Image】Copy to clipboard\nL65: \nL66:     @misc{cryptoeprint:2022/1763,\nL67:           author = {Liam Eagen and Dario Fiore and Ariel Gabizon},\nL68:           title = {cq: Cached quotients for fast lookups},\nL69:           howpublished = {Cryptology {ePrint} Archive, Paper 2022/1763},\nL70:           year = {2022},\nL71:           url = {https://eprint.iacr.org/2022/1763}\nL72:     }\nL73: \nL74: \nL75: Note: In order to protect the privacy of readers, eprint.iacr.org does not use cookies or embedded third party content.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReleases · Plonky3/Plonky3 · GitHub (https://github.com/Plonky3/Plonky3/releases)\nciteturn2view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.c